        "quiz_type": "single_choice",
        "question_type": "single_choice",
        "question_title": "For \\(f(x)=x^3-3x^2-9x+5\\), on which interval is \\(f\\) strictly decreasing?",
        "question_instruction": "Choose one correct option.",
        "explanation": "\\(f'(x)=3x^2-6x-9=3(x+1)(x-3)\\). Hence \\(f'(x)<0\\) for \\(-1<x<3\\), so \\(f\\) is strictly decreasing on \\((-1,3)\\).",
        "question_audio": null,
        "time_limit_seconds": 30,
        "points": 10,
        "sort_order": 161,
        "question_data": {
          "_meta": {
