        "question_title": "Evaluate \\(I=\\int_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}\\frac{dx}{1+\\tan x}\\).",
        "question_instruction": "Choose one correct option.",
        "explanation": "Replacing \\(x\\) by \\(\\frac{\\pi}{2}-x\\), the integrand becomes \\(\\frac{\\tan x}{1+\\tan x}\\). Their sum is \\(1\\). Therefore \\(2I=\\int_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}1\\,dx=\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\), giving \\(I=\\frac{\\pi}{4}\\).",
        "question_audio": null,
        "time_limit_seconds": 30,
        "points": 10,
        "sort_order": 162,
