        "question_title": "Find the area enclosed between the curves \\(y=x\\) and \\(y=x^2\\).",
        "question_instruction": "Choose one correct option.",
        "explanation": "The curves intersect at \\(x=0\\) and \\(x=1\\). On this interval, \\(x\\) lies above \\(x^2\\). Hence the area is \\(\\int_{0}^{1}(x-x^2)\\,dx=\\left[\\frac{x^2}{2}-\\frac{x^3}{3}\\right]_{0}^{1}=\\frac{1}{6}\\).",
